Task 1.4 Report

Research Methodology Statement

Executive Summary
A Personal Research & Documentation Standard was developed to define how research, documentation, evidence management, and version control will be maintained throughout the CloudMavin Cybersecurity Fellowship. The standard establishes consistent procedures for note-taking, file naming, source citation, evidence collection, and GitHub version control.

Objectives
• Establish a consistent research methodology.
• Define documentation standards.
• Standardize file naming conventions.
• Improve evidence management.
• Maintain version control using GitHub.
• Promote professional reporting practices.

Methodology
The methodology was developed by identifying best practices in cybersecurity documentation and adapting them to the fellowship requirements. Standards were created for note-taking, file organization, citation, version control, evidence management, and AI-assisted learning.

Technical Details

The standard covers:
• Note-taking
• File naming
• Documentation
• Source citation
• Version control
• Evidence management
• Backup strategy
• AI usage

Screenshots & Evidence
• Screenshot of the completed standard document in Obsidian.
• Screenshot of the GitHub repository after uploading the document.

Commands Used
No terminal commands were required for this task because it involved documentation and policy development.

Findings
A standardized documentation process improves organization, consistency, traceability, and the quality of cybersecurity reports.

Risk Rating
Low

Reason:
A documented methodology reduces the likelihood of losing evidence, creating inconsistent reports, or omitting important information.

Recommendations
• Follow the documentation standard consistently.
• Update the standard if new tools or workflows are adopted.
• Back up documentation regularly.
• Review documentation before submission.

Lessons Learned
This task highlighted the importance of maintaining structured documentation and version control throughout a cybersecurity project.

References
• NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0
• MITRE ATT&CK Framework
• NICE Workforce Framework
• GitHub Documentation
• Obsidian Documentation

AI Usage Declaration
Artificial Intelligence (ChatGPT by OpenAI) was used to explain documentation best practices and assist with report formatting. All decisions, organization, and final documentation were reviewed and approved by me
